  {
    "title": "A like crosses the ocean",
    "body": "A user in Europe clicks \"interested\". The EU copy counts it at once and sends it to the US a moment later, about 200 ms in all. A US user who loads the page 50 ms after the click still sees the **old count**, 1,203 instead of 1,204. A fraction of a second later both copies agree. This is **eventual consistency**: copies may disagree for a while but become the same when writes stop, and for a counter that is harmless.",
