  {
    "title": "One choice per feature",
    "body": "The same page uses both choices. Seats, payments and usernames choose **consistency**, because a wrong answer costs money or trust; the \"interested\" counter, reviews and feeds choose **availability**, because a slightly old value is harmless. A buyer's own tickets are read from the event's home region, so whenever that region can be reached they see the purchase they just made; during a partition a buyer across the break is asked to try again. Decide per feature by asking what a stale or conflicting answer would cost.",
